        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6f393fdd-6383-5f3f-894e-3d130fa78068",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Awki, Jacabamba, Andes, South America\n- Topics: Mountain ranges, glaciers, climatic regimes, prehistoric genera\n- Countries: Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Argentina, Chile\n- Organisms: Riograndia\n\nFacts:\n- Awki lies southeast of Jacabamba.\n- The Andes, also called the Andean Mountains or \"Cordillera de los Andes\" in Spanish, are the longest continental mountain range in the world.\n- The Andes extend north to south through Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Argentina, and Chile.\n- Glaciers in South America develop exclusively on the Andes.\n- Glaciers in South America are subject to the Andes' Tropical, Dry, and Wet climatic regimes.\n- Riograndia is a genus of tritheledontid cynodont from the Late Triassic of South America.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
